{
  "course": "初中60短文",
  "passage": 41,
  "title": "Passage 41",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s41-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p01.mp3",
      "en": "In China, there are 24 solar terms in a year.",
      "cn": "在中国，一年有24个节气。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s41-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p02.mp3",
      "en": "Six of them are in winter.",
      "cn": "其中有6个在冬季。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s41-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p03.mp3",
      "en": "They are Beginning of Winter, Light Snow, Heavy Snow, Winter Solstice, Lesser Cold and Greater Cold.",
      "cn": "它们是立冬、小雪、大雪、冬至、小寒和大寒。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s41-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p04.mp3",
      "en": "Beginning of Winter usually falls on November 7th or 8th, when people wear warm trousers to stay cozy.",
      "cn": "立冬通常在11月7日或8日，此时人们穿上暖和的裤子来保暖。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s41-p05-01",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p05-01.mp3",
      "en": "On this day, after a year of hard work,",
      "cn": "在这一天，经过一年的辛勤劳作，人们乐于休息一下，和家人们共度时光，包括他们的兄弟姐妹和堂（表）兄弟姐妹。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s41-p05-02",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p05-02.mp3",
      "en": "people are happy to have a rest and spend time with their families, including their brothers, sisters and cousins.",
      "cn": "在这一天，经过一年的辛勤劳作，人们乐于休息一下，和家人们共度时光，包括他们的兄弟姐妹和堂（表）兄弟姐妹。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s41-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p06.mp3",
      "en": "In ancient times, the northern part of China celebrated Beginning of Winter as the 'Small Spring Festival'.",
      "cn": "在古代，中国北方地区把立冬当作“小年”来庆祝。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s41-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p07.mp3",
      "en": "People usually had delicious dumplings and mutton soup on that day.",
      "cn": "那天，人们通常吃美味的饺子喝羊肉汤。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s41-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p08.mp3",
      "en": "Light Snow usually falls on November 22nd or 23rd and Heavy Snow usually falls on December 7th or 8th.",
      "cn": "小雪通常在11月22日或23日，大雪通常在12月7日或8日。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s41-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p09.mp3",
      "en": "When Winter Solstice comes, it brings the shortest day of the year and the longest night.",
      "cn": "冬至来临时，会伴随着一年中最短的白天和最长的夜晚。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s41-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p10.mp3",
      "en": "Many places around the country can expect the coldest weather.",
      "cn": "全国许多地方都会迎来最寒冷的天气。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s41-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p11.mp3",
      "en": "People usually cancel outdoor activities.",
      "cn": "人们通常会取消户外活动。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s41-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p12.mp3",
      "en": "When they go outside, they have to wear warm coats and scarves.",
      "cn": "外出时，他们需要穿上暖和的大衣，戴上围巾。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s41-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p13.mp3",
      "en": "Trees lose their leaves and the land looks dead.",
      "cn": "树木落叶，大地显得毫无生机。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s41-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p14.mp3",
      "en": "Farmers take care of their sheep and pigs, making sure they are safe in the cold.",
      "cn": "农民照顾他们的羊和猪，确保它们在寒冷中安全。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s41-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p15.mp3",
      "en": "Greater Cold comes after Lesser Cold.",
      "cn": "小寒过后是大寒。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s41-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p16.mp3",
      "en": "The field is covered with snow.",
      "cn": "田野被白雪覆盖。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s41-p17",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p17.mp3",
      "en": "And all Chinese are ready to welcome the Spring Festival after it.",
      "cn": "大寒过后，所有中国人都准备好迎接春节的到来。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s41-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p18.mp3",
      "en": "People take the lanterns and fireworks out, and children use scissors to make paper cuttings.",
      "cn": "人们拿出灯笼和烟花，孩子们用剪刀做剪纸。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 19,
      "chunkId": "s41-p19",
      "image": "assets/images/19.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s41-p19.mp3",
      "en": "Of course, a new round of solar terms will start.",
      "cn": "当然，新的一轮节气又将开始。"
    }
  ],
